//! One wasm module = the arora device + the Bevy view.
//!
//! The device is composed as `vizij-arora-web` composes it (arora 9 with no
//! default features over a `BlackboardStore`, a `RigHal` and a Vizij
//! `ProcessingGraph` built from the GLB's `VIZIJ_bundle`), owned by the Bevy
//! `App` as a non-send resource and stepped from `Update` with `Time::delta()`.
//! The view is the bevy-wasm spike's (a port of `crates/vizij/src/view.rs`):
//! it joins the spawned glTF scene with the `RobotData` bindings and applies
//! `RigHal::pose()` every frame. The GLB reaches Bevy from the bytes JS hands
//! over, through an in-memory asset source (`mem://face.glb`), never from
//! `assets/<path>`.
//!
//! JS surface (wasm-bindgen): `start(canvas, glbBytes)`, `setValue`,
//! `readValues`, `stop` (sends `AppExit`), `running`, `indexReady`, `poseLen`,
//! `frames`, `drainClicks` / `setClickCallback` (feature `picking`),
//! `spawnPlayViseme` / `halt` (the interpreter's SPAWN/HALT path).

